# x-use LLM settings. Copy this file to ".env" and fill in what you use.
#
# The LLM client is a single OpenAI-compatible client: one key, one base_url,
# one model covers OpenAI, OpenRouter, Azure, Gemini, and local servers
# (Ollama, vLLM) — they all speak the OpenAI chat-completions API.
#
# Precedence: environment variables (process env or this .env file) override
# the "llm" block in config/settings.json — env > settings.json. Placeholder
# values (e.g. "YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY") are rejected from BOTH sources, and
# with no valid key the client is simply not initialized (interactive MCP
# use needs no key — your agent writes the text).
# .env is gitignored; never commit real keys.
#
# Note: ${VAR} interpolation inside proxy strings in config/settings.json is a
# separate mechanism that reads the process environment — it remains
# proxy-strings-only and is unrelated to the settings below.

OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Examples: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1 (OpenRouter), http://localhost:11434/v1 (Ollama)
# Leave empty for api.openai.com.
OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# Examples: openai/gpt-4o-mini (OpenRouter), gpt-4o-mini (OpenAI), llama3.1 (Ollama)
OPENAI_MODEL=
